L000597	(b) Scaling exponents $\zeta(p)$ obtained from the relation $S_p(r) \propto \left\lbrack S_3(r) \right\rbrack^{\zeta(p)}$.
L000598	(c - f) $S_p(r)$ as a function of $S_3(r)$, where the vertical lines delimit the region $S_3(d_v) \le S_3(r) \le S_3(l_v)$. Solid lines are fits with $S_p(r) \propto \left\lbrack S_3(r) \right\rbrack^{\zeta(p)}$ 
L000599	using the whole range of $r$ in (a), i.e., $0.03 \le r \le 15$, 
L000600	where the fitted values of $\zeta(p)$ are the ones shown in (b). 
L000601	In all panels except (b), error bands and error bars represent one standard deviation. 
L000602	In panel (b), $\zeta(p)$ is computed by accounting for uncertainties in both $S_p(r)$ and $S_3(r)$, and the resulting error bars indicate the standard errors (i.e., the square roots of the diagonal elements of the covariance matrix) obtained from the orthogonal distance regression.
L000603	}
